   <div class="wrap narrow post-body prose">
 <h3><em>Learning to get into the Spirit together</em></h3><p>Family Matters · Part 3 · Ephesians 2–3</p>
+<aside class="mid-cta next-step"><div class="eyebrow">Your next step &middot; Free 8-day Bible plan</div><h3>Family Matters</h3><p>Eight days in Ephesians. Before Paul tells us how to live, he tells us what God has already done for us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.bible.com/reading-plans/79883-family-matters-eight-days-in-ephesians" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start the Plan in the Bible App <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></div></aside>
+
 
 <hr>
 
-<p>For two weeks we have been laying a foundation. Week one: you belong to Jesus, chosen and adopted before the foundation of the world. Last week: <em>we</em> belong to Jesus, and Paul prays constantly that the eyes of our hearts would be flooded with light to see the hope, the power, and the ascendancy of Christ that we share as a family.</p><p>Now Paul tells us what this family is <em>for</em>.</p><p><em>"So now you Gentiles are no longer strangers and foreigners. You are citizens along with all of God's holy people. You are members of God's family. Together, we are his house, built on the foundation of the apostles and the prophets. And the cornerstone is Christ Jesus himself. We are carefully joined together in him, becoming a holy temple for the Lord. Through him you Gentiles are also being made part of this dwelling where God lives by his Spirit."</em> (Ephesians 2:19–22, NLT)</p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
+<p>For two weeks we have been laying a foundation. Week one: you belong to Jesus, chosen and adopted before the foundation of the world. Last week: <em>we</em> belong to Jesus, and Paul prays constantly that the eyes of our hearts would be flooded with light to see the hope, the power, and the ascendancy of Christ that we share as a family.</p><p>Now Paul tells us what this family is <em>for</em>.</p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
 <form class="nl-form" action="https://gatecitybuckhead.us3.list-manage.com/subscribe/post?u=b941189c6bb50530d38f746fd&id=cdb1521460&f_id=00e92be2f0" method="post" target="_blank">
   <input type="hidden" name="tags" value="10814202,10812749"><div style="position:absolute;left:-5000px" aria-hidden="true"><input type="text" name="b_b941189c6bb50530d38f746fd_cdb1521460" tabindex="-1" value=""></div>
