-<p>In our knowledge-saturated culture, we've mastered the art of learning but often struggle with the discipline of doing. This disconnect between knowledge and action isn't just a modern problem—it's a timeless challenge that Jesus himself addressed in one of his most powerful parables.</p><p>THE FOUNDATION THAT MATTERS</p><p>In Jesus' final parable of the kingdom in the Sermon on the Mount, he tells the story of two builders: one who built his house on rock and another who built on sand. Jesus said:</p><p>"Therefore everyone who hears these words of mine and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock. The rain came down, the streams rose, and the winds blew and beat against that house; yet it did not fall, because it had its foundation on the rock. But everyone who hears these words of mine and does not put them into practice is like a foolish man who built his house on sand. The rain came down, the streams rose, and the winds blew and beat against that house, and it fell with a great crash." (Matthew 7:24-27)</p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
