+<p><strong>Metanoia, the Greek word translated "repentance," means a change of mind that leads to a change of direction.</strong> It joins <em>meta</em>, "after" or "change," with <em>nous</em>, "mind." When many people hear "repent," they hear "feel bad," guilty or ashamed. But metanoia is not mainly about feelings. It is turning: stopping, thinking again, and going a different way.</p>
+
