+
+<p><strong>Hallelujah means "praise Yah," a call to praise the Lord.</strong> It joins the Hebrew <em>hallelu</em>, "you all praise," with <em>Yah</em>, a short form of God's name, Yahweh. It is not just a feeling. It is an invitation: everyone, praise Him. The Psalms open and close with it, and the last five psalms each begin and end with it.</p>
