+<p style="margin-left:1.5em"><em>"Follow God's example, therefore, as dearly loved children and walk in the way of love, just as Christ loved us and gave himself up for us as a fragrant offering and sacrifice to God."</em> (Ephesians 5:1–2, NIV)</p>
+
 <p>Read that from the apex, because that is where Paul is standing. He is not handing down a code of conduct from a courtroom. He is describing, from the summit, what the children of God are like. Because of what Christ has done, who we are has fundamentally changed. Those who put off the fleshly works in chapter 4, who were renewed in the spirit of their minds and put on the new self, are now different. There has been a divine exchange, and it changes you from the inside out. So everything that follows in this chapter is not a ladder to climb. It is a family resemblance to grow into: dearly loved children, walking in the way of love, taking after the Father, imitating the Christ who gave himself for us. And the way we grow into it is the way it has been from the start of this letter: loving faith, leading to loving acts of obedience.</p>
 
