+<aside class="mid-cta next-step"><div class="eyebrow">Your next step &middot; Free 8-day Bible plan</div><h3>Family Matters</h3><p>Eight days in Ephesians. Before Paul tells us how to live, he tells us what God has already done for us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.bible.com/reading-plans/79883-family-matters-eight-days-in-ephesians" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start the Plan in the Bible App <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></div></aside>
+
 
 <hr>
 
 <p>Seven weeks ago we set out to climb a letter. Before we take the last steps, look back down the trail, because the view explains everything about where Paul chooses to end.</p>
 
-<p>In chapters 1 through 3 we learned who we are: blessed with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly realms, chosen before the foundation of the world, adopted as sons and daughters. We learned that we belong to Jesus, and that belonging made us family. In chapter 2, the family widened: the wall came down, strangers became citizens, and the household of God threw open its doors to everyone who comes by faith. In chapter 3, the mystery burst into full view: this family is not just a family. We are being built together into a dwelling place for God by his Spirit, a people designed to be filled with all the fullness of God.</p>
-
-<p>Then came the pivot of chapter 4: <em>therefore</em>. Walk worthy of the calling you have received. Put off the old self, be renewed in the spirit of your minds, put on the new. Chapter 5 took it higher: be imitators of God, as dearly loved children, and walk in love. Be holy as he is holy, not by effort but by faith. And last week we saw what imitating God actually produces: people so filled with the Spirit that it spills out of their mouths, speaking to one another with psalms, hymns, and songs from the Spirit, singing and making music from the heart. The overflowing life touches the tongue. That is one of the clearest fingerprints in all of Ephesians.</p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
