-<p><em>What does it mean to be truly blessed? And once we're blessed, what are we supposed to do with it?</em></p><p>These questions have haunted me for years as a pastor. I've watched people chase after blessing like it's the finish line—more money, bigger houses, better careers, perfect families. And I've watched them arrive at those destinations only to find themselves still empty, still restless, still asking, "Is this all there is?"</p><p>The problem isn't that we want to be blessed. God wants to bless us. The problem is that we've misunderstood what blessing is for.</p><p><strong><em>We think blessing is the destination. God knows it's the starting point.</em></strong></p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
+<p><em>What does it mean to be truly blessed? And once we're blessed, what are we supposed to do with it?</em></p>
+<aside class="mid-cta next-step"><div class="eyebrow">Your next step &middot; Free 7-day Bible plan</div><h3>Blessed to Be a Blessing</h3><p>Receiving from God and passing it on. God&#x27;s blessing is not meant to stop with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.bible.com/reading-plans/65940-blessed-to-be-a-blessing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start the Plan in the Bible App <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></div></aside>
+<p>These questions have haunted me for years as a pastor. I've watched people chase after blessing like it's the finish line—more money, bigger houses, better careers, perfect families. And I've watched them arrive at those destinations only to find themselves still empty, still restless, still asking, "Is this all there is?"</p><p>The problem isn't that we want to be blessed. God wants to bless us. The problem is that we've misunderstood what blessing is for.</p><aside class="mid-cta"><div class="eyebrow">The GateCity Buckhead Blog</div><h3>Get our weekly blog post right in your inbox.</h3><p>One new post each week from our pastors, plus what is happening at GateCity Buckhead.</p><div class="nl">
