+<p><strong>The Bible shows many types of prayer, and each one fits a different season of the soul.</strong> There is worship, when prayer sounds like praise. There is lament, when prayer sounds like grief. There is honest anger, when prayer sounds like a fight. And there is silence, when prayer has no words at all. Alongside these sit thanksgiving, confession, petition and intercession. God is not looking for one prayer tone. He is looking for honesty.</p>
