 <p><strong>A non-denominational church is a Christian church that is not part of, or governed by, a denomination such as Baptist, Methodist, Presbyterian, or Lutheran.</strong> It usually holds the core beliefs that Christians have always shared, like the authority of the Bible, the Trinity, and salvation through Jesus, but it sets its own leadership, practices, and statement of faith instead of receiving them from a denominational headquarters.</p>
