+<h3>Why Pray Together?</h3>
+
+<p>God has chosen prayer as one of the main ways He releases His power on the earth. Jesus Himself "always lives to make intercession" for us (Hebrews 7:25). When we pray, we join what He is already doing. At its simplest, intercession is telling God what He has told us to tell Him. It is simple enough for a child, and it is how God includes ordinary people in His work.</p>
+
 <p>Scripture even gives us a glimpse of heaven, where the prayers of God's people rise like incense before His throne (Revelation 5:8; 8:3-5). Your prayers matter there. And when believers gather and agree, something happens that doesn't happen alone.</p>
 
